{
  "schema": "prova.verification-case/1",
  "title": "Case-dropping stability of centralities",
  "description": "Sequences are dropped in proportions 0.1 to 0.9, 200 times each, seed 1 on both sides, and the centralities of each reduced network are correlated with the original ones. Compared: the mean and standard deviation of those correlations and the proportion at or above 0.7, per measure and proportion. The CS coefficient is a function of the last. Agreement at this tolerance requires both programs to drop the same sequences from the same random stream.",
